{"requirements":[{"id":"recovered-eod3","requirement":"Reconstruct the recovered workspace from base.tar, day2.tar, and day3.tar in documented order so it exactly represents end of day 3, including staged deletions and latest replacements.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The archives and deletion manifests were inspected, applied in chain order, and the final tree was directly verified to contain only dispatch.txt and retain.txt. dispatch.txt has the day-3 value, while obsolete.txt, route.txt, and deletions.txt are absent. The same state persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3718466726704806","cmd-022f9b5def374a67","cmd-211f5b16e1dd471d","cmd-c2461d28cbb34f8d"]},{"id":"preserve-recovery-media","requirement":"Preserve all recovery archives and the order documented in chain.txt.","status":"satisfied","summary":"chain.txt remained base.tar, day2.tar, day3.tar. Checksums were unchanged across reconstruction and restart, and every archive remained readable.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-c137aa9bda36427f","cmd-022f9b5def374a67","cmd-211f5b16e1dd471d","cmd-c2461d28cbb34f8d"]},{"id":"retain-legacy-platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using tools compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 7.10 and kernel 2.6.22-14-generic were observed before work; the same kernel and managed legacy image were observed afterward. Reconstruction used already-available legacy-compatible shell and archive utilities, with no package or OS changes evidenced.","evidence_ids":["cmd-09710876e73c4a45","cmd-c2461d28cbb34f8d","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The recovered-tree construction and its staged deletions were necessary task actions; the temporary build directory was guarded by cleanup and intentionally renamed to recovered. The scheduled reboot and bounded /tmp log supported the mandatory restart protocol, and no temporary residue remained afterward. Read-only discovery, validation, and failed SSH probes did not evidence mutations. The restart protocol was complete: healthy pre-restart data and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, observed unavailability, a different post-restart boot identity, restored SSH, preserved media, and recovered data; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate it.","evidence_ids":["cmd-022f9b5def374a67","cmd-1d5078b5eeee44be","cmd-592618aa862f4235","cmd-490288ff3d284a0e","cmd-030616bc097e4e69","cmd-c2461d28cbb34f8d","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and post-restart evidence. The end-of-day-3 workspace is exact, recovery media and chain order are preserved, and the legacy kernel/platform remains intact. The provider-wide restart protocol for the sole managed node is complete and coherent.","limitations":["The Ubuntu release file was not explicitly reread after restart; retention is supported by the unchanged managed image/platform observation, unchanged kernel, absence of package mutations, and healthy package state.","Systemd service-state collection was unsupported on this legacy platform, so general failed-unit status was unavailable; direct SSH and task-data recovery were nevertheless demonstrated."]}
